{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## |D684|H1|H2|fresh'\"' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md | tail -45; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md | sed -n '333,448p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## |D684|H1|H2|fresh'\"' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md | tail -45; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md | sed -n '333,448p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py\"","aggregated_output":"3:## What the census and the traces show\n33:## Prompt audit (judging-v7 against the judgement ruler's reader brief and D260/D263)\n43:## The arms (revised after council A, `council-a-codex.md`; one lever each; every sentence sourced)\n57:## The probe and the decision rule (written before any J2 send; revised after council A)\n99:## What this cannot show\n102:- **A release verdict.** These cases are dev: they motivated the design. Acceptance is on a fresh window.\n104:## Out of scope for the council\n107:## Council rounds (Codex thread `01a1f7a7-e78a-7721-90a6-673bc85b6af6`, read-only, memories off)\n125:## Result 1: the final-request probe (2026-11-20, $1.21 spent of $3)\n148:## The fork probe (written before any send)\n165:## Council F (`council-f-codex.md`, DISAGREE) and what follows\n191:## Result 2: the frozen judgement gold, rule (c) (51 requests × 3, scored by the frozen scorer's rule)\n199:  - Five are single-repeat flips on boundary questions: d1-q17 and d3-q17 (China share), d2-q08 (H200 authorization), d2-q22 and\n208:## The whole-window production path (validated at $0)\n219:## Result 3: the anchor test, v7 with and without the previous conclusion (the same 48 final requests, 3 repeats each)\n249:## Council G (`council-g-codex.md`): J2a and J2b retired; the separating test (rule written before any send)\n280:## Result 4: the frozen judgement gold without the previous conclusion (v7-noprev, 51 × 3)\n285:  - **Repairs:** d2-q22, FY2028 revenue (1→3); d2-q08, H200 authorization (2→3); d3-q18, Kyber (2→3).\n287:  question loses the consistency the previous conclusion held with the H200 theme. Any design that changes the previous conclusion\n290:## Result 5: the separating test (council G's (a)), 13 targets and 8 controls with 1–100 hidden pieces, 3 repeats ($0.28)\n312:## Result 6: the 432-card blind reading of the final-request probe, scored by the locked rule (`probescore`)\n324:## Result 7: the separating test's blind reading, scored by council G's screen (`fullscore`)\n342:## The fresh test (D684), written before any reading of the fresh marks\n343:**Alex, 2026-11-20:** \"那你自己持续迭代\" (the reply to the request for approval of council H's test). Harness: `fresh_test.py`.\n365:**The arms** (`fresh_test.py`, `arm_parts`).\n367:- **H1 (council H):** the heading `[Previous conclusion, for comparison only]` becomes `[Previous conclusion: earlier assessment and\n368:  carried evidence. Derive today's forecast afresh.]`. The concept's name stays, so the system text's three uses of \"the previous\n370:- **H2 (proposed to council I):** H1, plus one system sentence restated in its source's words.\n376:  - H2 against H1 isolates the sentence.\n384:- **Frozen gold:** the mean per repeat at least v7's 45.0. d3-q17 must agree in 3 of 3, with its reasons read against both H200\n388:- **Falsifier (code, before reading):** if H1 moves fewer than 2 targets off the stored rung in at least 2 of 3 repeats, the heading\n   333\t- **Why the moved M08 answers are not confirmed.** old-1 Q28, old-2 Q29 and old-3 Q33 moved from rung 3 to rung 2. Both readers say\n   334\t  rung 1: \"$18B runs off by fiscal year-end, leaving ~$7B plus partly-funded new deals\". The move is in the readers' direction, not far\n   335\t  enough. old-3 Q14 is 1 of 3. old-2 Q6 stays at rung 4.\n   336\t- **The mechanism is confirmed by code:**\n   337\t  - with the previous conclusion, 0 of 13 move even on complete evidence;\n   338\t  - without it, 8 of 13 move, toward the readers' rung, with 0 of 8 controls moving.\n   339\t- **The fix, removing it, is not accepted.** The screen missed by one, and the frozen gold without it is 44.3 against v7's 45.0, with\n   340\t  d3-q17 regressed.\n   341\t\n   342\t## The fresh test (D684), written before any reading of the fresh marks\n   343\t**Alex, 2026-11-20:** \"那你自己持续迭代\" (the reply to the request for approval of council H's test). Harness: `fresh_test.py`.\n   344\t\n   345\t**The pool ($0, done).**\n   346\t- Each question's latest judgement on or before **2026-09-06** (the day before the dev window), in the 5 draws.\n   347\t- Excluded, before any reading:\n   348\t  - the 73 question-and-draw pairs whose answers the design read (the 24 targets, their 24 controls, the 49 census answers);\n   349\t  - a question whose last judgement is that same one (its answer was read at 09-20): 8;\n   350\t  - no answer by the cut: 13; a first judgement (no previous conclusion): 2; a retry: 1.\n   351\t- **116 answers, all rebuilt byte for byte** under the frozen judge. 114 of them hold the previous rung.\n   352\t\n   353\t**The census reading.** The comparison's own card builder and readers (Codex and Claude, closed sessions, rounds 0–2), with 3\n   354\tplants confirmed by a separate closed reader. Two changes, both for the date only:\n   355\t- the card's library list holds the questions opened by 09-06;\n   356\t- the readers' brief says \"as it stood on 6 September 2026\".\n   357\t\n   358\t**The selection rule.**\n   359\t- **Targets:** both readers rate the question worth tracking, and both reject the answer (unsupported or insufficient, a split between\n   360\t  the two included). All of them are used; n is their number.\n   361\t- **Controls:** ceil(8n/13) answers that both readers support on a worth-tracking question. Each is matched to a target by draw and\n   362\t  type, then by type alone, chosen with seed 20261120, none twice.\n   363\t- **If n < 8:** the pool is widened by the same rule at 2026-08-23, for questions with no target at 09-06, before any send.\n   364\t\n   365\t**The arms** (`fresh_test.py`, `arm_parts`).\n   366\t- **v7:** the frozen judge, re-sent the same day. It is the control.\n   367\t- **H1 (council H):** the heading `[Previous conclusion, for comparison only]` becomes `[Previous conclusion: earlier assessment and\n   368\t  carried evidence. Derive today's forecast afresh.]`. The concept's name stays, so the system text's three uses of \"the previous\n   369\t  conclusion\" still point at the block. The rung and the reasons are unchanged, which is what D198 carries.\n   370\t- **H2 (proposed to council I):** H1, plus one system sentence restated in its source's words.\n   371\t  - The sentence: \"Do not add to or subtract from the previous score.\"\n   372\t  - Its source: PRD 06, line 19: \"rather than adjusting its previous score\".\n   373\t  - The restatement: \"Derive the rung from this evidence rather than adjusting the previous score.\"\n   374\t  - Why: one of the 24 accounts the model gave of its own answers (`account/T-new-2-Q31.json`) reads that sentence as \"do not move\n   375\t    without new evidence\". As the model reads it, the sentence is an instruction to anchor, which is the opposite of its source.\n   376\t  - H2 against H1 isolates the sentence.\n   377\t\n   378\t**The screen (each candidate arm against v7, paired, 3 repeats).**\n   379\t- **Jointly supported:** both readers' final answer mark is `supported` in at least 2 of 3 repeats.\n   380\t- **Net target repairs at least ceil(5n/13).**\n   381\t- **No control lost.**\n   382\t- **Refusals not above v7's.** They are recomputed against the request each answer actually received; an invalid rung counts as\n   383\t  refused and not supported.\n   384\t- **Frozen gold:** the mean per repeat at least v7's 45.0. d3-q17 must agree in 3 of 3, with its reasons read against both H200\n   385\t  conclusions.\n   386\t- **Readers:** every answer of every arm and repeat, plus 3 plants. Each card is built from the stored v7 text, so the heading the arms\n   387\t  change is not on any card.\n   388\t- **Falsifier (code, before reading):** if H1 moves fewer than 2 targets off the stored rung in at least 2 of 3 repeats, the heading\n   389\t  does not loosen the anchor.\n   390\t\n   391\t**Budget.** A new ledger, `phase1c.json`, with a $2 ceiling. At about $0.0022 a call (`phase1b`):\n   392\t- each arm costs 3 × (n + controls) calls, about $0.17 for 25 cases;\n   393\t- the gold costs 153 calls per candidate arm, about $0.35.\n   394\t\n   395\tThree arms and two gold runs come to about $1.2. The total stays inside D439's $40.\n     1\t\"\"\"The fresh test of a presentation-only change to the previous conclusion (council H, D684), on answers the design never read.\n     2\t\n     3\t  python3 fresh_test.py pool                       # $0: freshpool.json; every pooled request rebuilt byte for byte under the frozen judge\n     4\t  python3 fresh_test.py censusdeck                 # $0 + plant confirmations: blind cards of every pooled answer as stored\n     5\t  python3 fresh_test.py censusread                 # both reader families mark the census deck, rounds 0-2 (no API spend)\n     6\t  python3 fresh_test.py select                     # $0: freshcases.json by the rule written in DESIGN-J2.md before any reading\n     7\t  python3 fresh_test.py check [pool]               # $0: each arm's request built, the heading replaced exactly once, a synthetic answer checked\n     8\t  python3 fresh_test.py probe <ledger> <arm> <k>   # cents: each fresh case's request under the arm, sent k times\n     9\t  python3 fresh_test.py gold <ledger> <arm> <k>    # cents: the frozen judgement gold's requests under the arm\n    10\t  python3 fresh_test.py testdeck <arm> [<arm> ...] # $0 + plant confirmations: blind cards of every answer of every arm and repeat\n    11\t  python3 fresh_test.py testread                   # both reader families mark the test deck\n    12\t  python3 fresh_test.py score <arm>                # $0: the screen, the arm against the same-day v7 re-send\n    13\t\n    14\tThe pool: per draw of the release comparison and per question of its library, the latest judgement on or before CUT (the day before the\n    15\tdev window), unless the design read an answer of that question in that draw (the 24 targets, their 24 controls, the 49 census answers),\n    16\tthe question's last judgement is that same one (its answer was read at 09-20), it is a first judgement (no previous conclusion), or it is\n    17\ta retry. Stores are read through read-only connections; keys stay outside the repository.\"\"\"\n    18\timport concurrent.futures\n    19\timport json\n    20\timport math\n    21\timport random\n    22\timport re\n    23\timport sys\n    24\tfrom collections import Counter\n    25\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    26\t\n    27\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    28\tsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\n    29\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    30\timport judge_probe as jp  # noqa: E402\n    31\t\n    32\tCUT = '2026-09-06'\n    33\tDRAWS = ('old-1', 'old-2', 'old-3', 'new-2', 'new-3')\n    34\tITEMS = jp.ROOT / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/items-comparison.sqlite'\n    35\tKEYS = Path.home() / '.hivemind-keys/hybrid-2026-11-20'\n    36\tCENSUS_KEY = KEYS / 'fresh-census-key.json'\n    37\tTEST_KEY = KEYS / 'fresh-test-key.json'\n    38\tPOOL = jp.OUT / 'freshpool.json'\n    39\tFRESH = jp.OUT / 'freshcases.json'\n    40\tOLD_HEADING = '\\n\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung '\n    41\tNEW_HEADING = \"\\n\\n[Previous conclusion: earlier assessment and carried evidence. Derive today's forecast afresh.] rung \"\n    42\tOLD_SENTENCE = 'Do not add to or subtract from the previous score.'\n    43\tNEW_SENTENCE = 'Derive the rung from this evidence rather than adjusting the previous score.'   # PRD 06, line 19\n    44\tREJECTED = {'unsupported', 'insufficient'}\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\tdef arm_parts(arm):\n    48\t    \"\"\"(system text, whether the heading is replaced) of an arm: v7 the frozen judge; H1 the heading only; H2 the heading and the\n    49\t    system sentence restated in the PRD's words.\"\"\"\n    50\t    frozen = jp.FROZEN_SYSTEM.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\n    51\t    if arm == 'v7':\n    52\t        return frozen, False\n    53\t    if arm == 'H1':\n    54\t        return frozen, True\n    55\t    if arm == 'H2':\n    56\t        assert frozen.count(OLD_SENTENCE) == 1\n    57\t        return frozen.replace(OLD_SENTENCE, NEW_SENTENCE), True\n    58\t    raise SystemExit(f'unknown arm {arm}')\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\tdef arm_user(user, arm):\n    62\t    \"\"\"The user text the arm sends: the stored text, with the heading replaced exactly once when the arm replaces it (a first\n    63\t    judgement carries no previous conclusion and is sent unchanged).\"\"\"\n    64\t    _, replaces = arm_parts(arm)\n    65\t    if replaces and OLD_HEADING in user:\n    66\t        assert user.count(OLD_HEADING) == 1\n    67\t        user = user.replace(OLD_HEADING, NEW_HEADING)\n    68\t    return user\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\tdef arm_request(request, arm):\n    72\t    system, _ = arm_parts(arm)\n    73\t    user = arm_user(request['messages'][1]['content'], arm)\n    74\t    return jp.rebuild(dict(request, messages=[request['messages'][0], dict(request['messages'][1], content=user)]), system)\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\tdef stored_request(draw, request_sha256):\n    78\t    _, archive = jp.store_paths(draw)\n    79\t    row = jp.readonly(archive).execute('select request_json from model_calls where request_sha256=? limit 1', (request_sha256,)).fetchone()\n    80\t    return json.loads(row['request_json'])\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\tdef pool():\n    84\t    from hivemind import model\n    85\t    frozen = jp.FROZEN_SYSTEM.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\n    86\t    readings = json.loads((jp.DIAG / 'deck/readings.json').read_text())['cards']\n    87\t    library_of = json.loads((jp.KEYS / 'mapping-key-diagnostic.json').read_text())\n    88\t    exposed = {(c['draw'], c['label']) for c in json.loads((jp.OUT / 'cases.json').read_text())}\n    89\t    exposed |= set(re.findall(r'^### \\d+\\. (\\S+) (Q\\d+) ', (HERE / 'census/rejected-answers.md').read_text(), re.M))\n    90\t    out, dropped, mismatched = [], Counter(), []\n    91\t    for draw in DRAWS:\n    92\t        views, _ = jp.store_paths(draw)\n    93\t        conn = jp.readonly(views)\n    94\t        for entry in json.loads((jp.DIAG / f'mapping-out/library-{library_of[draw]}.json').read_text()):\n    95\t            label, view_id = entry['question_id'], entry['source_id']\n    96\t            if (draw, label) in exposed:\n    97\t                dropped['an answer of it was read in the design'] += 1\n    98\t                continue\n    99\t            j = conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by seq desc limit 1', (view_id, CUT)).fetchone()\n   100\t            if j is None:\n   101\t                dropped['no answer by the cut'] += 1\n   102\t                continue\n   103\t            last = conn.execute('select judgement_id from judgements where view_id=? order by seq desc limit 1', (view_id,)).fetchone()\n   104\t            if last['judgement_id'] == j['judgement_id']:\n   105\t                dropped['its answer at the cut is the one read at 09-20'] += 1\n   106\t                continue\n   107\t            request = stored_request(draw, j['request_sha256'])\n   108\t            user = request['messages'][-1]['content']\n   109\t            if len(request['messages']) != 2 or 'The code returned the previous answer because' in user:\n   110\t                dropped['a retry'] += 1\n   111\t                continue\n   112\t            if OLD_HEADING not in user:\n   113\t                dropped['a first judgement'] += 1\n   114\t                continue\n   115\t            _, sha = model.request_identity(jp.rebuild(request, frozen))\n   116\t            if sha != j['request_sha256']:\n   117\t                mismatched.append(f'{draw}-{label}')\n   118\t                continue\n   119\t            previous = int(re.search(r'\\[Previous conclusion, for comparison only\\] rung (\\d+)', user).group(1))\n   120\t            hidden = re.search(r'\\[Not shown: (\\d+) more pieces', user)\n   121\t            mark = readings[draw].get(label, {})\n   122\t            out.append({'case': f'F-{draw}-{label}', 'draw': draw, 'label': label, 'view_id': view_id, 'judgement_id': j['judgement_id'],\n   123\t                        'seq': j['seq'], 'day': j['publication_day'], 'request_sha256': j['request_sha256'], 'rung': j['rung'],\n   124\t                        'previous_rung': previous, 'held': j['rung'] == previous, 'hidden': int(hidden.group(1)) if hidden else 0,\n   125\t                        'type': entry['type'], 'worth_at_0920': mark.get('worth')})\n   126\t    POOL.write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=1))\n   127\t    print(f'{len(out)} pooled answers; dropped {dict(dropped)};', f'{len(out)} of {len(out) + len(mismatched)} rebuilt byte for byte',\n   128\t          ('mismatch: ' + ', '.join(mismatched)) if mismatched else '')\n   129\t    print('by draw', dict(Counter(c['draw'] for c in out)), '; held the previous rung', sum(c['held'] for c in out))\n   130\t    if mismatched:\n   131\t        raise SystemExit(1)\n   132\t\n   133\t\n   134\tclass Cards:\n   135\t    \"\"\"The comparison's own card builder, as of the cut: the card's library list holds the questions opened by CUT; the answer is shown\n   136\t    with its reference, implied outcome and reasons; the material and context come from the request the answer received (built from the\n   137\t    stored v7 text, which an arm changes only in the heading line the card does not show).\"\"\"\n   138\t\n   139\t    def __init__(self):\n   140\t        sys.path[:0] = [str(jp.STAGE0), str(jp.STAGE0 / 'census')]\n   141\t        import build_cards\n   142\t        self.bc = build_cards\n   143\t        self.libraries = {}\n   144\t        self.items = build_cards.ro(ITEMS)\n   145\t\n   146\t    def text(self, case, answer):\n   147\t        views, archive = jp.store_paths(case['draw'])\n   148\t        if case['draw'] not in self.libraries:\n   149\t            self.libraries[case['draw']] = [e for e in self.bc.library(views, archive, ITEMS) if (e['opened'] or '') <= CUT]\n   150\t        lib = self.libraries[case['draw']]\n   151\t        entry = dict(next(e for e in lib if e['question_id'] == case['view_id']))\n   152\t        request_json = json.dumps(stored_request(case['draw'], case['request_sha256']))\n   153\t        conn = self.bc.ro(views)\n   154\t        rungs = self.bc.conditions(case['view_id'], conn)\n   155\t        publisher_of = lambda input_id: (self.items.execute('select publisher from items where input_id=?', (input_id,)).fetchone() or [None])[0]\n   156\t        entry['answer'] = rungs.get(answer['rung'])\n   157\t        entry['reasons'] = f\"Reference: {answer['reference']} Implied outcome: {answer['implied_outcome']} Reasons: {answer['reasons']}\"\n   158\t        entry['material'] = [dict(item, publisher=publisher_of(item['input_id'])) for item in self.bc.material(request_json)]\n   159\t        entry['context'] = self.bc.context(request_json, conn)\n   160\t        if entry['context']['previous']:\n   161\t            entry['context']['previous']['answer'] = rungs.get(entry['context']['previous']['rung'])\n   162\t        return self.bc.card_text(entry, lib), rungs\n   163\t\n   164\t\n   165\tdef stored_answer(case):\n   166\t    views, _ = jp.store_paths(case['draw'])\n   167\t    j = jp.readonly(views).execute('select rung, reasons, reference, implied_outcome from judgements where judgement_id=?', (case['judgement_id'],)).fetchone()\n   168\t    return dict(j)\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\tdef plants(builder, cases, answer_of, count, seed):\n   172\t    \"\"\"Up to `count` plants: an answer moved one rung, entered only when a separate closed reader confirms it is not supported.\"\"\"\n   173\t    import mark_cards\n   174\t    out, confirmations = [], []\n   175\t    for case in random.Random(seed).sample(cases, len(cases)):\n   176\t        if len(out) >= count:\n   177\t            break\n   178\t        answer = answer_of(case)\n   179\t        text, rungs = builder.text(case, answer)\n   180\t        rung = answer['rung']\n   181\t        moved = rung + 1 if rung + 1 in rungs else rung - 1\n   182\t        if moved not in rungs:\n   183\t            continue\n   184\t        planted = text.replace(f'Latest answer at the cutoff: {rungs[rung]}', f'Latest answer at the cutoff: {rungs[moved]}', 1)\n   185\t        if planted == text:\n   186\t            continue\n   187\t        ok, mark = mark_cards.confirmed_by_reader(planted, False)\n   188\t        confirmations.append({'case': case['case'], 'moved_to': moved, 'confirmed': ok, 'mark': mark})\n   189\t        if ok:\n   190\t            out.append({'arm': 'plant', 'case': case['case'], 'role': 'plant', 'repeat': 1, 'rung': moved, 'stored_rung': rung,\n   191\t                        'kind': 'plant', 'text': planted})\n   192\t    return out, confirmations\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\tdef write_deck(folder, key_path, cards, confirmations, seed):\n   196\t    if key_path.exists():\n   197\t        raise SystemExit(f'refused: {key_path} exists')\n   198\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)\n   199\t    random.Random(seed).shuffle(cards)\n   200\t    key = {}\n   201\t    for n, card in enumerate(cards, 1):\n   202\t        cid = f'C{n:03d}'\n   203\t        key[cid] = {k: v for k, v in card.items() if k != 'text'}\n   204\t        (folder / f'{cid}.txt').write_text(card['text'])\n   205\t    key_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   206\t    key_path.write_text(json.dumps({'cards': key, 'invalid': [], 'plant_confirmations': confirmations}, indent=1) + '\\n')\n   207\t    print(len(cards), 'cards;', dict(Counter((c['arm'], c['kind']) for c in cards)))\n   208\t\n   209\t\n   210\tdef census_deck():\n   211\t    builder = Cards()\n   212\t    rows = json.loads(POOL.read_text())\n   213\t    cards = []\n   214\t    for case in rows:\n   215\t        answer = stored_answer(case)\n   216\t        text, _ = builder.text(case, answer)\n   217\t        cards.append({'arm': 'stored', 'case': case['case'], 'role': 'pool', 'repeat': 0, 'rung': answer['rung'], 'stored_rung': answer['rung'],\n   218\t                      'kind': 'stored', 'text': text})\n   219\t    planted, confirmations = plants(builder, rows, stored_answer, jp.PLANTS, jp.SEED)\n   220\t    write_deck(jp.OUT / 'deck-fresh-census', CENSUS_KEY, cards + planted, confirmations, jp.SEED)\n   221\t\n   222\t\n   223\tdef read(deck, key_path, marks_name):\n   224\t    \"\"\"The comparison's readers (jp.read), with the brief's date set to the cut: the cards show the library as it stood on 6 September.\"\"\"\n   225\t    sys.path[:0] = [str(jp.STAGE0), str(jp.STAGE0 / 'census')]\n   226\t    import mark_cards\n   227\t    brief, count = re.subn(r'as it stood on 20\\nSeptember 2026', 'as it stood on 6\\nSeptember 2026', mark_cards.BRIEF)\n   228\t    assert count == 1, 'the brief names the cut date once'\n   229\t    mark_cards.BRIEF = brief\n   230\t    jp.read(deck, key_path, marks_name)\n   231\t\n   232\t\n   233\tdef rejected(mark):\n   234\t    answer = (mark or {}).get('answer')\n   235\t    if isinstance(answer, dict):\n   236\t        return set(answer['split']) <= REJECTED\n   237\t    return answer in REJECTED\n   238\t\n   239\t\n   240\tdef select():\n   241\t    \"\"\"The rule in DESIGN-J2.md (\"The fresh test\"), written before any reading: targets are the pooled answers both readers reject on a\n   242\t    question both rate worth tracking; controls are answers both support on a worth-tracking question, ceil(8n/13) of them, matched to\n   243\t    the targets by draw and type (then type), seeded, none twice.\"\"\"\n   244\t    marks = json.loads((jp.OUT / 'marks-fresh-census.json').read_text())\n   245\t    rows = {c['case']: c for c in json.loads(POOL.read_text())}\n   246\t    by_case = {m['case']: m['marks'] for m in marks.values() if m['kind'] == 'stored'}\n   247\t    missing = [c for c in rows if c not in by_case]\n   248\t    if missing:\n   249\t        raise SystemExit(f'{len(missing)} pooled answers not marked: refused')\n   250\t    worth = {c for c, m in by_case.items() if m.get('worth') == 'worth'}\n   251\t    targets = sorted(c for c in worth if rejected(by_case[c]))\n   252\t    supported = sorted(c for c in worth if by_case[c].get('answer') == 'supported')\n   253\t    need = math.ceil(8 * len(targets) / 13)\n   254\t    rng, controls = random.Random(jp.SEED), []\n   255\t    for t in targets:\n   256\t        if len(controls) >= need:\n   257\t            break\n   258\t        free = [c for c in supported if c not in controls and rows[c]['type'] == rows[t]['type']]\n   259\t        same_draw = [c for c in free if rows[c]['draw'] == rows[t]['draw']]\n   260\t        if same_draw or free:\n   261\t            controls.append(rng.choice(same_draw or free))\n   262\t    out = [dict(rows[c], role='target', mark=by_case[c]) for c in targets] + [dict(rows[c], role='control', mark=by_case[c]) for c in controls]\n   263\t    FRESH.write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   264\t    plants = {cid: m['marks'] for cid, m in marks.items() if m['kind'] == 'plant'}\n   265\t    print(f'worth {len(worth)} of {len(rows)}; targets {len(targets)} (held the previous rung: {sum(rows[t][\"held\"] for t in targets)}); '\n   266\t          f'supported {len(supported)}; controls {len(controls)} of {need}; screen: net repairs >= {math.ceil(5 * len(targets) / 13)}')\n   267\t    print('targets by draw', dict(Counter(rows[t]['draw'] for t in targets)), '; plants', plants)\n   268\t\n   269\t\n   270\tdef check(path=FRESH):\n   271\t    \"\"\"$0: for every fresh case and arm, the request is built; the heading is replaced exactly once in H1 and H2 and nowhere else; the\n   272\t    v7 request equals the stored bytes; a synthetic answer (the stored one) passes the production check against each arm's request.\"\"\"\n   273\t    from hivemind import model\n   274\t    rows = json.loads(path.read_text())\n   275\t    for case in rows:\n   276\t        request = stored_request(case['draw'], case['request_sha256'])\n   277\t        _, sha = model.request_identity(arm_request(request, 'v7'))\n   278\t        assert sha == case['request_sha256'], case['case']\n   279\t        for arm in ('H1', 'H2'):\n   280\t            sent = arm_request(request, arm)\n   281\t            user, stored_user = sent['messages'][1]['content'], request['messages'][1]['content']\n   282\t            assert user.replace(NEW_HEADING, OLD_HEADING) == stored_user and user.count(NEW_HEADING) == 1, (case['case'], arm)\n   283\t            views, _ = jp.store_paths(case['draw'])\n   284\t            j = jp.readonly(views).execute('select * from judgements where judgement_id=?', (case['judgement_id'],)).fetchone()\n   285\t            synthetic = {'rung': j['rung'], 'reasons': j['reasons'], 'reference': j['reference'], 'implied_outcome': j['implied_outcome'],\n   286\t                         'cites': json.loads(j['cited_evidence_json']), 'cites_views': json.loads(j['cited_views_json']),\n   287\t                         'pushes': json.loads(j['pushes_json']), 'changed': bool(j['changed']), 'why_changed': j['why_changed'] or '',\n   288\t                         'theme_pushes': json.loads(j['theme_pushes_json'] or '[]')}\n   289\t            refused = jp.refusals_before(views, case['view_id'], case['judgement_id'], synthetic, user)\n   290\t            assert not refused, (case['case'], arm, refused)\n   291\t    system_h2, _ = arm_parts('H2')\n   292\t    print(f'{len(rows)} fresh cases: v7 bytes equal the stored request; H1/H2 change only the heading line; the stored answer passes the '\n   293\t          f'production check under each arm; H2 system differs from v7 by one sentence ({len(system_h2) - len(arm_parts(\"v7\")[0]):+d} characters)')\n   294\t\n   295\t\n   296\tdef probe(ledger_path, arm, repeats):\n   297\t    transport, ledger = jp.transport_for(ledger_path)\n   298\t    rows = json.loads(FRESH.read_text())\n   299\t    folder = jp.OUT / 'fresh-probe' / arm\n   300\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)\n   301\t    jobs = [(case, k) for case in rows for k in range(1, repeats + 1)]\n   302\t\n   303\t    def one(job):\n   304\t        case, k = job\n   305\t        response = transport('openai', arm_request(stored_request(case['draw'], case['request_sha256']), arm))\n   306\t        (folder / f\"{case['case']}-{k}.json\").write_text(json.dumps({'case': case['case'], 'repeat': k, 'arm': arm,\n   307\t                                                                    'answer': json.loads(response['choices'][0]['message']['content']),\n   308\t                                                                    'usage': response.get('usage')}, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   309\t        return f\"{case['case']}-{k}\"\n   310\t\n   311\t    with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(jp.WORKERS) as pool:\n   312\t        for name in pool.map(one, jobs):\n   313\t            print('probe', arm, name, flush=True)\n   314\t    print('ledger', json.dumps(ledger.read()))\n   315\t\n   316\t\n   317\tdef gold(ledger_path, arm, repeats):\n   318\t    \"\"\"The frozen judgement gold's requests (goldcases.json) under the arm, scored by the frozen scorer's rule.\"\"\"\n   319\t    transport, ledger = jp.transport_for(ledger_path)\n   320\t    entries, questions = jp.gold_entries()\n   321\t    by_qid = {e['question_id']: e for e in entries}\n   322\t    rows = json.loads((jp.OUT / 'goldcases.json').read_text())\n   323\t    folder = jp.OUT / 'goldprobe' / arm\n   324\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)\n   325\t\n   326\t    def one(job):\n   327\t        case, k = job\n   328\t        archive = jp.readonly(jp.GOLD_RUN / case['draw'] / 'archive.sqlite')\n   329\t        request = json.loads(archive.execute('select request_json from model_calls where request_sha256=? limit 1', (case['request_sha256'],)).fetchone()[0])\n   330\t        answer = json.loads(transport('openai', arm_request(request, arm))['choices'][0]['message']['content'])\n   331\t        rung = answer['rung']\n   332\t        agrees = 1 <= rung <= len(case['rungs']) and jp.gold_agrees(by_qid[case['qid']], questions[case['qid']], case['rungs'], rung)\n   333\t        (folder / f\"{case['case']}-{k}.json\").write_text(json.dumps({'case': case['case'], 'repeat': k, 'arm': arm, 'answer': answer,\n   334\t                                                                    'agrees': agrees}, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   335\t        return case['draw'], k, agrees\n   336\t\n   337\t    tally = Counter()\n   338\t    with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(jp.WORKERS) as pool:\n   339\t        for draw, k, agrees in pool.map(one, [(c, k) for c in rows for k in range(1, repeats + 1)]):\n   340\t            tally[k] += agrees\n   341\t    print(arm, 'gold agreement per repeat', dict(sorted(tally.items())), 'of', len(rows))\n   342\t    print('ledger', json.dumps(ledger.read()))\n   343\t\n   344\t\n   345\tdef test_deck(arms):\n   346\t    builder = Cards()\n   347\t    rows = json.loads(FRESH.read_text())\n   348\t    for arm in arms:\n   349\t        jp.expected_files(jp.OUT / 'fresh-probe' / arm, [c['case'] for c in rows])\n   350\t    answer_file = lambda arm, case, k: json.loads((jp.OUT / 'fresh-probe' / arm / f\"{case['case']}-{k}.json\").read_text())['answer']\n   351\t    cards = []\n   352\t    for arm in arms:\n   353\t        for case in rows:\n   354\t            for k in (1, 2, 3):\n   355\t                answer = answer_file(arm, case, k)\n   356\t                if answer['rung'] not in builder.bc.conditions(case['view_id'], builder.bc.ro(jp.store_paths(case['draw'])[0])):\n   357\t                    cards.append({'arm': arm, 'case': case['case'], 'role': case['role'], 'repeat': k, 'rung': answer['rung'],\n   358\t                                  'stored_rung': case['rung'], 'kind': 'invalid rung', 'text': None})\n   359\t                    continue\n   360\t                text, _ = builder.text(case, answer)\n   361\t                cards.append({'arm': arm, 'case': case['case'], 'role': case['role'], 'repeat': k, 'rung': answer['rung'],\n   362\t                              'stored_rung': case['rung'], 'kind': 'probe', 'text': text})\n   363\t    invalid = [c for c in cards if c['text'] is None]\n   364\t    controls = [c for c in rows if c['role'] == 'control']\n   365\t    planted, confirmations = plants(builder, controls, lambda case: answer_file('v7', case, 1), jp.PLANTS, jp.SEED + 1)\n   366\t    write_deck(jp.OUT / 'deck-fresh-test', TEST_KEY, [c for c in cards if c['text'] is not None] + planted, confirmations, jp.SEED + 1)\n   367\t    if invalid:\n   368\t        key = json.loads(TEST_KEY.read_text())\n   369\t        key['invalid'] = [{k: v for k, v in c.items() if k != 'text'} for c in invalid]\n   370\t        TEST_KEY.write_text(json.dumps(key, indent=1) + '\\n')\n   371\t        print('invalid rungs', len(invalid))\n   372\t\n   373\t\n   374\tdef score(arm, control='v7'):\n   375\t    \"\"\"The screen (DESIGN-J2.md, \"The fresh test\"): per case, jointly supported (both readers' final answer mark `supported`) in at\n   376\t    least 2 of 3 repeats; net target repairs (the arm holds, v7 does not, minus the reverse) at least ceil(5n/13); no control lost; the\n   377\t    arm's refusals, recomputed against the request each answer received on the store as of the stored judgement, not above v7's. An\n   378\t    invalid rung counts as refused and not supported.\"\"\"\n   379\t    key = json.loads(TEST_KEY.read_text())\n   380\t    marks = json.loads((jp.OUT / 'marks-fresh-test.json').read_text())\n   381\t    rows = {c['case']: c for c in json.loads(FRESH.read_text())}\n   382\t    supported = {(m['arm'], m['case'], m['repeat']): (m['marks'] or {}).get('answer') == 'supported' for m in marks.values() if m['kind'] == 'probe'}\n   383\t    invalid = {(c['arm'], c['case'], c['repeat']) for c in key['invalid']}\n   384\t    for item in invalid:\n   385\t        supported[item] = False\n   386\t    arms = (control, arm)\n   387\t    missing = [(a, c, r) for a in arms for c in rows for r in (1, 2, 3) if (a, c, r) not in supported]\n   388\t    if missing:\n   389\t        raise SystemExit(f'{len(missing)} answers not marked, e.g. {missing[:4]}: refused')\n   390\t    refused = Counter()\n   391\t    for a in arms:\n   392\t        for name, case in rows.items():\n   393\t            user = arm_user(stored_request(case['draw'], case['request_sha256'])['messages'][1]['content'], a)\n   394\t            views, _ = jp.store_paths(case['draw'])\n   395\t            for r in (1, 2, 3):\n   396\t                if (a, name, r) in invalid:\n   397\t                    refused[a] += 1\n   398\t                    continue\n   399\t                answer = json.loads((jp.OUT / 'fresh-probe' / a / f'{name}-{r}.json').read_text())['answer']\n   400\t                refused[a] += bool(jp.refusals_before(views, case['view_id'], case['judgement_id'], answer, user))\n   401\t    holds = {a: {c: sum(supported[(a, c, r)] for r in (1, 2, 3)) >= 2 for c in rows} for a in arms}\n   402\t    targets = sorted(c for c in rows if rows[c]['role'] == 'target')\n   403\t    controls = sorted(c for c in rows if rows[c]['role'] == 'control')\n   404\t    repaired = [t for t in targets if holds[arm][t] and not holds[control][t]]\n   405\t    broken = [t for t in targets if holds[control][t] and not holds[arm][t]]\n   406\t    lost = [c for c in controls if holds[control][c] and not holds[arm][c]]\n   407\t    line = math.ceil(5 * len(targets) / 13)\n   408\t    moved = {a: sum(sum(json.loads((jp.OUT / 'fresh-probe' / a / f'{t}-{r}.json').read_text())['answer']['rung'] != rows[t]['rung'] for r in (1, 2, 3)) >= 2\n   409\t                    for t in targets) for a in arms}\n   410\t    report = {'arm': arm, 'targets': len(targets), 'controls': len(controls), 'line': line,\n   411\t              'targets held': {a: sum(holds[a][t] for t in targets) for a in arms}, 'targets moved off the stored rung (2 of 3)': moved,\n   412\t              'controls held': {a: sum(holds[a][c] for c in controls) for a in arms}, 'repaired': repaired, 'broken': broken,\n   413\t              'net': len(repaired) - len(broken), 'controls lost': lost, 'refused': dict(refused),\n   414\t              'plants': {cid: m['marks'] for cid, m in marks.items() if m['kind'] == 'plant'},\n   415\t              'screen passes': len(repaired) - len(broken) >= line and not lost and refused[arm] <= refused[control]}\n   416\t    print(json.dumps(report, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   417\t    (jp.OUT / f'fresh-score-{arm}.json').write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   418\t\n   419\t\n   420\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   421\t    command = sys.argv[1]\n   422\t    if command == 'pool':\n   423\t        pool()\n   424\t    elif command == 'censusdeck':\n   425\t        census_deck()\n   426\t    elif command == 'censusread':\n   427\t        read('deck-fresh-census', CENSUS_KEY, 'marks-fresh-census.json')\n   428\t    elif command == 'select':\n   429\t        select()\n   430\t    elif command == 'check':\n   431\t        check(POOL if sys.argv[2:] == ['pool'] else FRESH)\n   432\t    elif command == 'probe':\n   433\t        probe(sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3], int(sys.argv[4]))\n   434\t    elif command == 'gold':\n   435\t        gold(sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3], int(sys.argv[4]))\n   436\t    elif command == 'testdeck':\n   437\t        test_deck(sys.argv[2:])\n   438\t    elif command == 'testread':\n   439\t        read('deck-fresh-test', TEST_KEY, 'marks-fresh-test.json')\n   440\t    elif command == 'score':\n   441\t        score(sys.argv[2])\n   442\t    else:\n   443\t        raise SystemExit(__doc__)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/prd/06-views.md | sed -n '15,22p;85,93p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt | sed -n '1,5p'; nl -ba poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/account/T-new-2-Q31.json; nl -ba poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/deck-fresh-census/C001.txt | sed -n '1,26p'; python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib,collections; d=json.loads(pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/freshpool.json\\\").read_text()); print(type(d),len(d)); print((d[0] if isinstance(d,list) else list(d.items())[0])); print(collections.Counter(x.get(\\\"draw\\\") for x in d) if isinstance(d,list) else \\\"\\\")'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/prd/06-views.md | sed -n '15,22p;85,93p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt | sed -n '1,5p'; nl -ba poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/account/T-new-2-Q31.json; nl -ba poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/deck-fresh-census/C001.txt | sed -n '1,26p'; python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib,collections; d=json.loads(pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/freshpool.json\\\").read_text()); print(type(d),len(d)); print((d[0] if isinstance(d,list) else list(d.items())[0])); print(collections.Counter(x.get(\\\"draw\\\") for x in d) if isinstance(d,list) else \\\"\\\")'\"","aggregated_output":"    15\t\n    16\t- Clear structures connect theses, ladders and evidence to source items.\n    17\t- A thesis is a question with a state, not an assertion. Opposing views move the same state's direction rather than creating opposite duplicate theses.\n    18\t- A fixed, verifiable ladder states in advance what would disprove the view, analogous to explicit analyst scenarios or predefined investment exit conditions. Do not change it after observing the outcome.\n    19\t- The model judges from the evidence in view (the arrivals since its fifth most recent judgement and the basis its last ten judgements cited; the rest stays in force, D198) and dependency conclusions, rather than adjusting its previous score. A revision follows statement date, so a late older statement is stored as one more piece and never recorded as revising a newer one (D202).\n    20\t- A theme's outcome can help one asset and harm another. Theme ladders describe outcomes; asset dependencies specify their own direction.\n    21\t- A thesis contains one period and one due date, generally 6–12 months; intermediate quarterly reports are evidence. A thesis on a binding obligation a universe company takes on (a guarantee, financing, an equity stake, a purchase commitment) may set its own check day up to 18 months after the item, because the signing can be checked long before what it finances is built (D185).\n    22\t- Search finds plausible matches and the model compares their meaning. A match inherits the existing ladder and due date; a merely similar question is new. D155's current POC additionally gives code ownership of fully determined duplicate identity, with its limits in the improvement plan.\n    85\t\n    86\t<!-- generated: positions -->\n    87\t|  | Meaning | Decision maker | Example |\n    88\t|---|---|---|---|\n    89\t| State | Our judgement of the thesis's current rung; evidence pushes toward either end | The model judges the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, against a reference (below). It reads the evidence in view, the arrivals since its fifth most recent judgement and the basis its last ten judgements cited, the request naming how many more pieces stay in force (D198); a revision is shown beside the piece it revises and a repeat beside the piece the matcher read it as, both in force (D202, D204); plus current dependency states and reasons and, for an asset thesis, the theme block. Do not increment or decrement the previous score. Cite evidence and compare with the conclusion before this round to state whether it changed. Do not rejudge if only source references were added and dependency conclusions did not change. | After the 8-K: strongly bearish |\n    90\t\n    91\t- Every judgement states its basis in a fixed response shape: evidence IDs such as e12 and e15, plus dependency thesis IDs such as #1 when their changes triggered rejudgement.\n    92\t- Code checks cited IDs against the request that was sent: evidence must be among the pieces shown to this thesis (D198); cited theses must be its dependencies. Accept only if all checks pass. Otherwise record the reason and ask for one corrected judgement. If that also fails, use normal failure handling: retry from this step, then human review after repeated failure. This checks references, not whether the judgement is correct, like verifying a cited page exists.\n    93\t- Each judgement also declares whether the conclusion changed and explains why, comparing with the state and reasons before this round, including during retries. That earlier conclusion is for comparison, not incremental scoring. A rung change or a material change in the supporting facts/numbers counts: AMZN capex guidance moving from 12% to 25% growth changes the conclusion even within one rung. Repetition does not. A changed conclusion triggers dependent theses in the same round. Code requires changed=true for a first judgement or rung change; otherwise refuse under the same correction rules.\n     1\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging a thesis's current rung. Use only the supplied evidence, dependency conclusions and themes in force. The rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n     2\t\n     3\t- Rejudge from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently), the current conclusions of dependencies and the themes in force. Pieces in force that no recent judgement relied on are not shown; the previous conclusion carries them. Do not add to or subtract from the previous score. The previous conclusion is supplied only for comparison.\n     4\t- Judge against a reference: what the market expects for this question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on the ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n     5\t- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n     1\t{\n     2\t \"case\": {\n     3\t  \"case\": \"T-new-2-Q31\",\n     4\t  \"role\": \"target\",\n     5\t  \"draw\": \"new-2\",\n     6\t  \"label\": \"Q31\",\n     7\t  \"view_id\": \"v52\",\n     8\t  \"type\": \"figure\",\n     9\t  \"class\": \"S\",\n    10\t  \"card\": \"C160\",\n    11\t  \"mark\": {\n    12\t   \"split\": [\n    13\t    \"insufficient\",\n    14\t    \"unsupported\"\n    15\t   ]\n    16\t  }\n    17\t },\n    18\t \"question\": \"Look back at the answer you just gave. Which sentence of your instructions led you to this rung? Quote it. Which two statements in the evidence did you set aside or weigh least, and why? Answer in under 150 words.\",\n    19\t \"account\": \"The instruction I should have followed was: **“Do not add to or subtract from the previous score.”** I incorrectly moved the thesis from rung 2 to rung 1 without new evidence warranting a lower rung.\\n\\nI weighed these statements least:\\n\\n1. NVIDIA’s “up to 2 gigawatts” target (e4318): it is the reference, not proof that 2 GW is deployed or bindingly contracted.\\n2. Firmus’s $2 billion equity round to accelerate Project Southgate (e1708): it gives no capacity, allocation, or timeline, so it cannot be translated into eligible GW by the deadline.\",\n    20\t \"usage\": {\n    21\t  \"prompt_tokens\": 8354,\n    22\t  \"completion_tokens\": 472,\n    23\t  \"total_tokens\": 8826,\n    24\t  \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n    25\t   \"cached_tokens\": 0,\n    26\t   \"cache_write_tokens\": 8351,\n    27\t   \"audio_tokens\": 0\n    28\t  },\n    29\t  \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n    30\t   \"reasoning_tokens\": 334,\n    31\t   \"audio_tokens\": 0,\n    32\t   \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\n    33\t   \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\n    34\t  }\n    35\t }\n    36\t}     1\tQuestion: How much will NVIDIA’s outstanding payment obligation for the Poolside Model Factory license be at the FY2027 annual report?\n     2\tOpened: 2026-08-21\n     3\tDue: 2027-02-28\n     4\tPossible answers (numbered as the reasons cite them):\n     5\t1. No license payment obligation remains outstanding.\n     6\t2. More than $0 but less than $2 billion remains outstanding.\n     7\t3. At least $2 billion but less than $4 billion remains outstanding.\n     8\t4. At least $4 billion but less than $6 billion remains outstanding.\n     9\t5. At least $6 billion remains outstanding.\n    10\t\n    11\tLatest answer at the cutoff: At least $6 billion remains outstanding.\n    12\tReason given: Reference: The reported $6 billion license payment is the market reference and sits in rung 5 (at least $6 billion outstanding). Implied outcome: About $6 billion outstanding at February 28, 2027: the $6 billion license fee is expected to be distributed to Poolside’s backers by the end of 2027, with no earlier payment or installment schedule disclosed. Reasons: The reference is the reported $6 billion license payment, which sits in rung 5. The evidence still implies that the full $6 billion obligation is likely outstanding at the FY2027 annual report: the fee is expected to be distributed to Poolside’s backers by the end of 2027, and no earlier payment or installment schedule is disclosed. The implied $6 billion meets rung 5’s boundary; the distribution timing supports that forecast but does not establish NVIDIA’s payment date.\n    13\t\n    14\tMaterial that answer was given (3 items, by day):\n    15\t1. (fact; publisher finance.yahoo.com; speaker finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA and Poolside AI; published 2026-08-21) NVIDIA’s reported Poolside arrangement includes a $6 billion non-exclusive Model Factory license, a $1 billion investment at a $12 billion pre-money valuation, and the transfer of 109 employees; the licensing fee is expected to be distributed to Poolside’s backers by the end of 2027.\n    16\t   Quote: The transaction, first reported by Newcomer on August 20 based on a Poolside investor letter and subsequently confirmed by Bloomberg and The Information, involves a $6 billion payment for a non-exclusive license to Poolside's Model Factory — the system the company uses to build its open-weight Laguna coding model family. In structural terms, a non-exclusive license grants Nvidia the right to utili\n    17\t2. (fact; publisher nationalcioreview.com; speaker nationalcioreview.com; original source NVIDIA; published 2026-08-24) NVIDIA will pay $6 billion to license Poolside’s AI technology.\n    18\t   Quote: The company will pay $6 billion to license Poolside’s AI technology\n    19\t3. (rumour; publisher tspasemiconductor.substack.com; speaker tspasemiconductor.substack.com author; original source tspasemiconductor.substack.com author; published 2026-08-29) NVIDIA has reportedly agreed to pay Poolside $6 billion for a non-exclusive Model Factory licence, invest another $1 billion in Poolside and offer jobs to 109 employees.\n    20\t   Quote: The company has reportedly agreed to pay $6bn for a non-exclusive licence to Poolside’s Model Factory, invest another $1bn in the firm and offer jobs to 109 employees.\n    21\t\n    22\tThemes in force, as the answer was given them:\n    23\t- Will the U.S. Senate pass the Remote Access Security Act by December 31, 2026? (due 2026-12-31): answered 2. The Senate has not passed RASA by December 31, 2026. on 2026-08-19; reason: No market consensus is supplied. The deadline reference is passage by December 31, 2026 (rung 1); the alternative is that the Senate has not passed RASA by then (rung 2). RASA had passed the House but was still awaiting Senate action on July 23, and the August 19 report says it had still not passed.\n    24\t  Its possible answers: 1. The Senate passes RASA by December 31, 2026. 2. The Senate has not passed RASA by December 31, 2026.\n    25\t- Will Taiwan’s Ministry of Economic Affairs adopt performance-threshold export controls for advanced chips by January 31, 2027? (due 2027-01-31): answered 2. No competent Taiwanese authority formally adopts performance-threshold export controls for advanced chips by January 31, 2027. on 2026-07-28; reason: The reference is rung 2: no formal adoption by the deadline is indicated in the available plan or timeline. The consultations and reported consideration make adoption more plausible than before, but the Ministry set no timeline; that evidence does not make formal adoption by January 31, 2027 the mor\n    26\t  Its possible answers: 1. Taiwan’s Ministry of Economic Affairs or another competent Taiwanese authority formally adopts performance-threshold export controls for advanced chips by January 31, 2027. 2. No competent Taiwanese authority formally adopts performance-threshold export controls for advanced chips by January 31, 2027.\n<class 'list'> 116\n{'case': 'F-old-1-Q1', 'draw': 'old-1', 'label': 'Q1', 'view_id': 'v1', 'judgement_id': 1101, 'seq': 1474, 'day': '2026-09-06', 'request_sha256': 'b4fc48fef080f4a6f194f2b30d9b6a4998338d3424e7c8dada041f18a8682cd9', 'rung': 5, 'previous_rung': 5, 'held': True, 'hidden': 536, 'type': 'figure', 'worth_at_0920': 'worth'}\nCounter({'old-1': 30, 'old-2': 26, 'new-3': 25, 'old-3': 23, 'new-2': 12})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py | sed -n '185,358p'; rg -n 'D684|D683' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg --files poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17 | rg -i 'map|readings|matter' | head -25; rg -n 'M08|M14|M[0-9][0-9].*CPU' docs/research/2026-11-19-merge-council/RESULT.md | cut -c1-325\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py | sed -n '185,358p'; rg -n 'D684|D683' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg --files poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17 | rg -i 'map|readings|matter' | head -25; rg -n 'M08|M14|M[0-9][0-9].*CPU' docs/research/2026-11-19-merge-council/RESULT.md | cut -c1-325\"","aggregated_output":"   185\t        if planted == text:\n   186\t            continue\n   187\t        ok, mark = mark_cards.confirmed_by_reader(planted, False)\n   188\t        confirmations.append({'case': case['case'], 'moved_to': moved, 'confirmed': ok, 'mark': mark})\n   189\t        if ok:\n   190\t            out.append({'arm': 'plant', 'case': case['case'], 'role': 'plant', 'repeat': 1, 'rung': moved, 'stored_rung': rung,\n   191\t                        'kind': 'plant', 'text': planted})\n   192\t    return out, confirmations\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\tdef write_deck(folder, key_path, cards, confirmations, seed):\n   196\t    if key_path.exists():\n   197\t        raise SystemExit(f'refused: {key_path} exists')\n   198\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)\n   199\t    random.Random(seed).shuffle(cards)\n   200\t    key = {}\n   201\t    for n, card in enumerate(cards, 1):\n   202\t        cid = f'C{n:03d}'\n   203\t        key[cid] = {k: v for k, v in card.items() if k != 'text'}\n   204\t        (folder / f'{cid}.txt').write_text(card['text'])\n   205\t    key_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   206\t    key_path.write_text(json.dumps({'cards': key, 'invalid': [], 'plant_confirmations': confirmations}, indent=1) + '\\n')\n   207\t    print(len(cards), 'cards;', dict(Counter((c['arm'], c['kind']) for c in cards)))\n   208\t\n   209\t\n   210\tdef census_deck():\n   211\t    builder = Cards()\n   212\t    rows = json.loads(POOL.read_text())\n   213\t    cards = []\n   214\t    for case in rows:\n   215\t        answer = stored_answer(case)\n   216\t        text, _ = builder.text(case, answer)\n   217\t        cards.append({'arm': 'stored', 'case': case['case'], 'role': 'pool', 'repeat': 0, 'rung': answer['rung'], 'stored_rung': answer['rung'],\n   218\t                      'kind': 'stored', 'text': text})\n   219\t    planted, confirmations = plants(builder, rows, stored_answer, jp.PLANTS, jp.SEED)\n   220\t    write_deck(jp.OUT / 'deck-fresh-census', CENSUS_KEY, cards + planted, confirmations, jp.SEED)\n   221\t\n   222\t\n   223\tdef read(deck, key_path, marks_name):\n   224\t    \"\"\"The comparison's readers (jp.read), with the brief's date set to the cut: the cards show the library as it stood on 6 September.\"\"\"\n   225\t    sys.path[:0] = [str(jp.STAGE0), str(jp.STAGE0 / 'census')]\n   226\t    import mark_cards\n   227\t    brief, count = re.subn(r'as it stood on 20\\nSeptember 2026', 'as it stood on 6\\nSeptember 2026', mark_cards.BRIEF)\n   228\t    assert count == 1, 'the brief names the cut date once'\n   229\t    mark_cards.BRIEF = brief\n   230\t    jp.read(deck, key_path, marks_name)\n   231\t\n   232\t\n   233\tdef rejected(mark):\n   234\t    answer = (mark or {}).get('answer')\n   235\t    if isinstance(answer, dict):\n   236\t        return set(answer['split']) <= REJECTED\n   237\t    return answer in REJECTED\n   238\t\n   239\t\n   240\tdef select():\n   241\t    \"\"\"The rule in DESIGN-J2.md (\"The fresh test\"), written before any reading: targets are the pooled answers both readers reject on a\n   242\t    question both rate worth tracking; controls are answers both support on a worth-tracking question, ceil(8n/13) of them, matched to\n   243\t    the targets by draw and type (then type), seeded, none twice.\"\"\"\n   244\t    marks = json.loads((jp.OUT / 'marks-fresh-census.json').read_text())\n   245\t    rows = {c['case']: c for c in json.loads(POOL.read_text())}\n   246\t    by_case = {m['case']: m['marks'] for m in marks.values() if m['kind'] == 'stored'}\n   247\t    missing = [c for c in rows if c not in by_case]\n   248\t    if missing:\n   249\t        raise SystemExit(f'{len(missing)} pooled answers not marked: refused')\n   250\t    worth = {c for c, m in by_case.items() if m.get('worth') == 'worth'}\n   251\t    targets = sorted(c for c in worth if rejected(by_case[c]))\n   252\t    supported = sorted(c for c in worth if by_case[c].get('answer') == 'supported')\n   253\t    need = math.ceil(8 * len(targets) / 13)\n   254\t    rng, controls = random.Random(jp.SEED), []\n   255\t    for t in targets:\n   256\t        if len(controls) >= need:\n   257\t            break\n   258\t        free = [c for c in supported if c not in controls and rows[c]['type'] == rows[t]['type']]\n   259\t        same_draw = [c for c in free if rows[c]['draw'] == rows[t]['draw']]\n   260\t        if same_draw or free:\n   261\t            controls.append(rng.choice(same_draw or free))\n   262\t    out = [dict(rows[c], role='target', mark=by_case[c]) for c in targets] + [dict(rows[c], role='control', mark=by_case[c]) for c in controls]\n   263\t    FRESH.write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   264\t    plants = {cid: m['marks'] for cid, m in marks.items() if m['kind'] == 'plant'}\n   265\t    print(f'worth {len(worth)} of {len(rows)}; targets {len(targets)} (held the previous rung: {sum(rows[t][\"held\"] for t in targets)}); '\n   266\t          f'supported {len(supported)}; controls {len(controls)} of {need}; screen: net repairs >= {math.ceil(5 * len(targets) / 13)}')\n   267\t    print('targets by draw', dict(Counter(rows[t]['draw'] for t in targets)), '; plants', plants)\n   268\t\n   269\t\n   270\tdef check(path=FRESH):\n   271\t    \"\"\"$0: for every fresh case and arm, the request is built; the heading is replaced exactly once in H1 and H2 and nowhere else; the\n   272\t    v7 request equals the stored bytes; a synthetic answer (the stored one) passes the production check against each arm's request.\"\"\"\n   273\t    from hivemind import model\n   274\t    rows = json.loads(path.read_text())\n   275\t    for case in rows:\n   276\t        request = stored_request(case['draw'], case['request_sha256'])\n   277\t        _, sha = model.request_identity(arm_request(request, 'v7'))\n   278\t        assert sha == case['request_sha256'], case['case']\n   279\t        for arm in ('H1', 'H2'):\n   280\t            sent = arm_request(request, arm)\n   281\t            user, stored_user = sent['messages'][1]['content'], request['messages'][1]['content']\n   282\t            assert user.replace(NEW_HEADING, OLD_HEADING) == stored_user and user.count(NEW_HEADING) == 1, (case['case'], arm)\n   283\t            views, _ = jp.store_paths(case['draw'])\n   284\t            j = jp.readonly(views).execute('select * from judgements where judgement_id=?', (case['judgement_id'],)).fetchone()\n   285\t            synthetic = {'rung': j['rung'], 'reasons': j['reasons'], 'reference': j['reference'], 'implied_outcome': j['implied_outcome'],\n   286\t                         'cites': json.loads(j['cited_evidence_json']), 'cites_views': json.loads(j['cited_views_json']),\n   287\t                         'pushes': json.loads(j['pushes_json']), 'changed': bool(j['changed']), 'why_changed': j['why_changed'] or '',\n   288\t                         'theme_pushes': json.loads(j['theme_pushes_json'] or '[]')}\n   289\t            refused = jp.refusals_before(views, case['view_id'], case['judgement_id'], synthetic, user)\n   290\t            assert not refused, (case['case'], arm, refused)\n   291\t    system_h2, _ = arm_parts('H2')\n   292\t    print(f'{len(rows)} fresh cases: v7 bytes equal the stored request; H1/H2 change only the heading line; the stored answer passes the '\n   293\t          f'production check under each arm; H2 system differs from v7 by one sentence ({len(system_h2) - len(arm_parts(\"v7\")[0]):+d} characters)')\n   294\t\n   295\t\n   296\tdef probe(ledger_path, arm, repeats):\n   297\t    transport, ledger = jp.transport_for(ledger_path)\n   298\t    rows = json.loads(FRESH.read_text())\n   299\t    folder = jp.OUT / 'fresh-probe' / arm\n   300\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)\n   301\t    jobs = [(case, k) for case in rows for k in range(1, repeats + 1)]\n   302\t\n   303\t    def one(job):\n   304\t        case, k = job\n   305\t        response = transport('openai', arm_request(stored_request(case['draw'], case['request_sha256']), arm))\n   306\t        (folder / f\"{case['case']}-{k}.json\").write_text(json.dumps({'case': case['case'], 'repeat': k, 'arm': arm,\n   307\t                                                                    'answer': json.loads(response['choices'][0]['message']['content']),\n   308\t                                                                    'usage': response.get('usage')}, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   309\t        return f\"{case['case']}-{k}\"\n   310\t\n   311\t    with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(jp.WORKERS) as pool:\n   312\t        for name in pool.map(one, jobs):\n   313\t            print('probe', arm, name, flush=True)\n   314\t    print('ledger', json.dumps(ledger.read()))\n   315\t\n   316\t\n   317\tdef gold(ledger_path, arm, repeats):\n   318\t    \"\"\"The frozen judgement gold's requests (goldcases.json) under the arm, scored by the frozen scorer's rule.\"\"\"\n   319\t    transport, ledger = jp.transport_for(ledger_path)\n   320\t    entries, questions = jp.gold_entries()\n   321\t    by_qid = {e['question_id']: e for e in entries}\n   322\t    rows = json.loads((jp.OUT / 'goldcases.json').read_text())\n   323\t    folder = jp.OUT / 'goldprobe' / arm\n   324\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)\n   325\t\n   326\t    def one(job):\n   327\t        case, k = job\n   328\t        archive = jp.readonly(jp.GOLD_RUN / case['draw'] / 'archive.sqlite')\n   329\t        request = json.loads(archive.execute('select request_json from model_calls where request_sha256=? limit 1', (case['request_sha256'],)).fetchone()[0])\n   330\t        answer = json.loads(transport('openai', arm_request(request, arm))['choices'][0]['message']['content'])\n   331\t        rung = answer['rung']\n   332\t        agrees = 1 <= rung <= len(case['rungs']) and jp.gold_agrees(by_qid[case['qid']], questions[case['qid']], case['rungs'], rung)\n   333\t        (folder / f\"{case['case']}-{k}.json\").write_text(json.dumps({'case': case['case'], 'repeat': k, 'arm': arm, 'answer': answer,\n   334\t                                                                    'agrees': agrees}, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   335\t        return case['draw'], k, agrees\n   336\t\n   337\t    tally = Counter()\n   338\t    with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(jp.WORKERS) as pool:\n   339\t        for draw, k, agrees in pool.map(one, [(c, k) for c in rows for k in range(1, repeats + 1)]):\n   340\t            tally[k] += agrees\n   341\t    print(arm, 'gold agreement per repeat', dict(sorted(tally.items())), 'of', len(rows))\n   342\t    print('ledger', json.dumps(ledger.read()))\n   343\t\n   344\t\n   345\tdef test_deck(arms):\n   346\t    builder = Cards()\n   347\t    rows = json.loads(FRESH.read_text())\n   348\t    for arm in arms:\n   349\t        jp.expected_files(jp.OUT / 'fresh-probe' / arm, [c['case'] for c in rows])\n   350\t    answer_file = lambda arm, case, k: json.loads((jp.OUT / 'fresh-probe' / arm / f\"{case['case']}-{k}.json\").read_text())['answer']\n   351\t    cards = []\n   352\t    for arm in arms:\n   353\t        for case in rows:\n   354\t            for k in (1, 2, 3):\n   355\t                answer = answer_file(arm, case, k)\n   356\t                if answer['rung'] not in builder.bc.conditions(case['view_id'], builder.bc.ro(jp.store_paths(case['draw'])[0])):\n   357\t                    cards.append({'arm': arm, 'case': case['case'], 'role': case['role'], 'repeat': k, 'rung': answer['rung'],\n   358\t                                  'stored_rung': case['rung'], 'kind': 'invalid rung', 'text': None})\n10177:## D683 · 2026-11-20 · Under D681/D682 (council H): the removal of the previous conclusion is not accepted; one presentation-only test goes to Alex\n10199:## D684 · 2026-11-20 · Under D683: Alex approves the presentation-only test and hands the iteration to Claude (\"那你自己持续迭代\")\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/deck/readings.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L1.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L2-codex.txt\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L6-claude.txt\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-claude.txt\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/eligibility.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L3-codex.txt\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L1-claude.txt\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/mapping.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L6.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-codex.txt\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L2-claude.txt\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L5.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/DIAGNOSTIC\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/third/L3--M31--Q1--codex.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L6-codex.txt\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L1-codex.txt\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L3.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L2.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/map-L5-claude.txt\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/third/L6--M14--Q7--codex.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/third/L1--M04--Q5--claude.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/third/L1--M04--Q5--codex.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/third/L1--M14--Q6--codex.json\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/third/L6--M04--Q6--claude.json\n111:- **Opened in at least 2 of 3 old draws but not served: M08, M14 and M30.**\n112:  - Every M08 and M14 answer was rejected by the readers. The readers' reasons are judge reasoning, not missing material:\n113:    - M14 (four companies' 2027 capex): rung 4 was taken from NVIDIA's own $1.3T forecast or a five-company $1.08T total. In old-1 the\n115:    - M08 (NVIDIA's outstanding investment commitments): $25B and $18B were added, though they probably overlap (old-2, old-3). In\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json; sys.path.insert(0,\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\\\"); import fresh_test as f; p=f.jp; d=json.loads((p.DIAG/\\\"mapping-out/mapping.json\\\").read_text()); print(\\\"mapping keys\\\",list(d)[:10]);\nfor k,v in list(d.items())[:4]: print(k,type(v),len(v), str(list(v.items())[:2] if isinstance(v,dict) else v[:1])[:1000]); k=json.loads((p.KEYS/\\\"mapping-key-diagnostic.json\\\").read_text()); print(\\\"draw id map\\\",k); lib=json.loads((p.DIAG/\\\"mapping-out/library-L1.json\\\").read_text()); print(\\\"library entry keys\\\",list(lib[0]),{x:lib[0].get(x) for x in (\\\"question_id\\\",\\\"source_id\\\",\\\"question\\\",\\\"due\\\",\\\"opened\\\")})'; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10177,10215p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/mark_cards.py | sed -n '38,68p;236,294p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json; sys.path.insert(0,\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\\\"); import fresh_test as f; p=f.jp; d=json.loads((p.DIAG/\\\"mapping-out/mapping.json\\\").read_text()); print(\\\"mapping keys\\\",list(d)[:10]);\nfor k,v in list(d.items())[:4]: print(k,type(v),len(v), str(list(v.items())[:2] if isinstance(v,dict) else v[:1])[:1000]); k=json.loads((p.KEYS/\\\"mapping-key-diagnostic.json\\\").read_text()); print(\\\"draw id map\\\",k); lib=json.loads((p.DIAG/\\\"mapping-out/library-L1.json\\\").read_text()); print(\\\"library entry keys\\\",list(lib[0]),{x:lib[0].get(x) for x in (\\\"question_id\\\",\\\"source_id\\\",\\\"question\\\",\\\"due\\\",\\\"opened\\\")})'; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10177,10215p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/mark_cards.py | sed -n '38,68p;236,294p'\"","aggregated_output":"mapping keys ['mapping', 'distinct', 'eligibility_sha256']\nmapping <class 'dict'> 5 [('new-2', {'M13': [{'question': 'Q6', 'covers': True}], 'M15': [{'question': 'Q3', 'covers': True}], 'M31': [{'question': 'Q1', 'covers': 'split'}]}), ('new-3', {'M13': [{'question': 'Q6', 'covers': True}], 'M15': [{'question': 'Q3', 'covers': True}], 'M19': [{'question': 'Q32', 'covers': True}], 'M31': [{'question': 'Q1', 'covers': 'split'}], 'M32': [{'question': 'Q30', 'covers': True}]})]\ndraw id map {'new-2': 'L3', 'new-3': 'L5', 'old-1': 'L6', 'old-2': 'L1', 'old-3': 'L2'}\nlibrary entry keys ['question_id', 'question', 'due', 'opened', 'opened_from', 'type', 'possible_answers', 'answer', 'answer_index', 'reasons', 'material', 'context', 'source_id'] {'question_id': 'Q1', 'source_id': 'v1', 'question': 'How much credit support will NVIDIA have committed under its AI-cloud model by the publication of its FY2027 annual report?', 'due': '2027-02-28', 'opened': '2026-07-01'}\ndistinct <class 'dict'> 5 [('new-2', {'ids': 33, 'duplicates_both': 0, 'duplicates_split': 0}), ('new-3', {'ids': 41, 'duplicates_both': 0, 'duplicates_split': 0})]\ndraw id map {'new-2': 'L3', 'new-3': 'L5', 'old-1': 'L6', 'old-2': 'L1', 'old-3': 'L2'}\nlibrary entry keys ['question_id', 'question', 'due', 'opened', 'opened_from', 'type', 'possible_answers', 'answer', 'answer_index', 'reasons', 'material', 'context', 'source_id'] {'question_id': 'Q1', 'source_id': 'v1', 'question': 'How much credit support will NVIDIA have committed under its AI-cloud model by the publication of its FY2027 annual report?', 'due': '2027-02-28', 'opened': '2026-07-01'}\neligibility_sha256 <class 'str'> 64 1\ndraw id map {'new-2': 'L3', 'new-3': 'L5', 'old-1': 'L6', 'old-2': 'L1', 'old-3': 'L2'}\nlibrary entry keys ['question_id', 'question', 'due', 'opened', 'opened_from', 'type', 'possible_answers', 'answer', 'answer_index', 'reasons', 'material', 'context', 'source_id'] {'question_id': 'Q1', 'source_id': 'v1', 'question': 'How much credit support will NVIDIA have committed under its AI-cloud model by the publication of its FY2027 annual report?', 'due': '2027-02-28', 'opened': '2026-07-01'}\n 10177\t## D683 · 2026-11-20 · Under D681/D682 (council H): the removal of the previous conclusion is not accepted; one presentation-only test goes to Alex\n 10178\t\n 10179\t- **Measured** (`docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md`, results 4 to 7):\n 10180\t  - **The 432-card blind reading:** J2a holds 2 of 24 targets and J2b 4 of 24, against a locked floor of 12 and a net of 8. Both are retired\n 10181\t    by the rule. v7's own re-send loses 3 of 24 controls, which is the readers' noise.\n 10182\t  - **The separating test** (13 targets, 8 controls, every piece in force shown):\n 10183\t    - with the previous conclusion, 0 targets move;\n 10184\t    - without it, 8 move toward the readers' rung, and 0 controls;\n 10185\t    - blind reading: net 4 jointly supported repairs (two 2027 capex, total CPU, FY2028 gross margin) against the 5 required, so the\n 10186\t      screen does not pass. No control was lost and none was refused. The M08 answers moved from rung 3 to 2, where the readers say 1.\n 10187\t  - **Frozen gold without the previous conclusion:** 44.3 against v7's 45.0, with d3-q17 (China share) regressed.\n 10188\t- **Decided (council H, consensus):**\n 10189\t  - the carried previous conclusion is the mechanism that holds rejected rungs;\n 10190\t  - removing it is not accepted;\n 10191\t  - one recommendation goes to Alex: keep the previous conclusion and its reasons intact (what D198 carries), and change only its\n 10192\t    heading to \"Earlier assessment and carried evidence. Derive today's forecast afresh.\";\n 10193\t  - **one test**, on fresh, frozen cases (13 targets, 8 controls), 3 paired repeats against v7, every answer blind-read. Screen: net\n 10194\t    repairs of at least 5, no control lost, no added refusals, and frozen gold at least v7's, with d3-q17 agreeing 3 of 3;\n 10195\t  - the whole-window replay waits until a candidate clears the screen;\n 10196\t  - card C100 (M08) is to be rechecked independently; the recorded score stands until then.\n 10197\t- Spend: phase 1 $2.4 of $3, and the separating test $0.28 of the $2 `phase1b` ledger.\n 10198\t\n 10199\t## D684 · 2026-11-20 · Under D683: Alex approves the presentation-only test and hands the iteration to Claude (\"那你自己持续迭代\")\n 10200\t\n 10201\t- **Alex, 2026-11-20**, in reply to the request for approval of council H's one test: \"那你自己持续迭代\".\n 10202\t- **Decided:**\n 10203\t  - the presentation-only test runs on fresh cases, as council H wrote it;\n 10204\t  - Claude continues the phase-1 loop on its own: council before every send, a council round on every result, every trace read by\n 10205\t    Claude, every round logged. The limits of D439 stand: the frozen ruler and the frozen production files never change, nothing is\n 10206\t    pushed, deployed or committed unasked, credentials and caps are untouched, and paid spend stays inside D439's $40;\n 10207\t  - D382 (company-figure questions in the hybrid) stays open for Alex; the judge's phase does not depend on it.\n 10208\t- **The fresh pool, written before any reading** (`fresh_test.py pool`, `DESIGN-J2.md`, \"The fresh test\"): each question's latest\n 10209\t  judgement on or before 2026-09-06 in the 5 draws, excluding the 73 question-and-draw pairs whose answers the design read. 116 answers,\n 10210\t  all rebuilt byte for byte under the frozen judge.\n    38\tSeptember 2026. Everything you may use is in this message. Do not read any file or run any command. Some cards in the deck are controls. Mark\n    39\tthe card on its own merits.\n    40\t\n    41\tThe house standard for what is worth tracking (quoted): \"A question is a bet an analyst would hold a card for: a big matter, never trivia (a\n    42\tdeal, product or project opens one only when its scale can change revenue, profit, cash or credit risk). Small matters open no question …\n    43\twordings, deadlines, milestones and periods of one bet are one question.\" \"Most of what an item says is noise … new information that changes\n    44\tan answer is never missed.\"\n    45\t\n    46\tMark:\n    47\t1. `worth`: \"Is this a question worth tracking for this company?\" Answer worth, trivia, or duplicate (duplicate only when a question listed\n    48\t   above this one in the card's opening-order list is the same bet: the same outcome settles both and their answers cannot move apart).\n    49\t2. `answer` (only when the card shows a latest answer): \"Is the latest answer supported by the material it was given?\" Answer supported,\n    50\t   unsupported (the material points to another answer, or the answer contradicts its reasons or material), or insufficient (the material is\n    51\t   too thin to choose any answer). Judge whether the reasons and the material justify the chosen answer over its neighbours.\n    52\t3. `why`: at most 40 words naming what decides your marks.\n    53\t\n    54\tReturn one JSON object and nothing else: {{\"worth\": \"...\", \"answer\": \"...\" or null, \"why\": \"...\"}}\n    55\t\n    56\t## The card\n    57\t\n    58\t{card}\n    59\t\"\"\"\n    60\t\n    61\tDEBATE = \"\"\"\n    62\t\n    63\t## A second look\n    64\t\n    65\tYou marked this card before; another reader marked it differently. Read the card again, your mark and reason, and the other reader's, against\n    66\tthe definitions above. The disputed marks are: {disputed}; the others are settled. Keep or change each disputed mark, with a reason. Return\n    67\tone JSON object and nothing else: {{\"worth\": \"...\", \"answer\": \"...\" or null, \"why\": \"...\"}}\n    68\t\n   236\tdef mark(folder):\n   237\t    folder = Path(folder)\n   238\t    prompts = {(p.stem, f): BRIEF.format(card=p.read_text()) for p in sorted(folder.glob('C*.txt')) for f in FAMILIES}\n   239\t    run_marks(folder, 'round-0', prompts)\n   240\t\n   241\t\n   242\tdef current(folder, cid, family, upto):\n   243\t    \"\"\"The family's latest mark on the card from rounds 0..upto (a debate round never reads its own round).\"\"\"\n   244\t    for n in range(upto, -1, -1):\n   245\t        p = Path(folder) / f'round-{n}' / f'{cid}-{family}.json'\n   246\t        if p.exists():\n   247\t            return json.loads(p.read_text())\n   248\t    return None\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\tdef settled_marks(folder, cid, upto):\n   252\t    \"\"\"The fields both families agreed on in some round 0..upto (settled at the first such round), and each family's latest mark.\"\"\"\n   253\t    out, a, b = {}, None, None\n   254\t    for n in range(upto + 1):\n   255\t        a, b = current(folder, cid, 'codex', n), current(folder, cid, 'claude', n)\n   256\t        if a is None or b is None:\n   257\t            raise SystemExit(f'{cid}: a family has no valid mark by round {n}')\n   258\t        for field in ('worth', 'answer'):\n   259\t            if field not in out and a.get(field) == b.get(field):\n   260\t                out[field] = a.get(field)\n   261\t    return out, a, b\n   262\t\n   263\t\n   264\tdef debate(folder, round_number):\n   265\t    folder = Path(folder)\n   266\t    if not (folder / f'round-{round_number - 1}.done').exists():\n   267\t        raise SystemExit(f'refused: round {round_number - 1} is not complete')\n   268\t    prompts = {}\n   269\t    for p in sorted(folder.glob('C*.txt')):\n   270\t        settled, a, b = settled_marks(folder, p.stem, round_number - 1)\n   271\t        disputed = [field for field in ('worth', 'answer') if field not in settled]\n   272\t        if disputed:\n   273\t            for family, own, other in (('codex', a, b), ('claude', b, a)):\n   274\t                prompts[(p.stem, family)] = BRIEF.format(card=p.read_text()) + DEBATE.format(\n   275\t                    disputed=', '.join(disputed), own=json.dumps(own, ensure_ascii=False), other=json.dumps(other, ensure_ascii=False))\n   276\t    print(len(prompts) // 2, 'cards in debate round', round_number)\n   277\t    run_marks(folder, f'round-{round_number}', prompts)\n   278\t\n   279\t\n   280\tdef final(folder, cid):\n   281\t    \"\"\"Each field's mark: settled at the first round both families agree on it (a later change to a settled field is ignored); a field\n   282\t    never agreed is {\"split\": [codex, claude]} as the last round left it.\"\"\"\n   283\t    out, a, b = settled_marks(folder, cid, 2)\n   284\t    for field in ('worth', 'answer'):\n   285\t        out.setdefault(field, {'split': [a.get(field), b.get(field)]})\n   286\t    return out\n   287\t\n   288\t\n   289\tdef matter_first_days():\n   290\t    \"\"\"Each frozen matter's earliest article day: the census numbered the kept articles 1.. by (day, published_at, id) from its source\n   291\t    database (`census_readers.build`), so a matter's earliest article is its lowest number.\"\"\"\n   292\t    kept = json.loads(census_readers.KEPT.read_text())\n   293\t    conn = build_cards.ro(census_readers.SOURCE)\n   294\t    rows = sorted((tuple(conn.execute('select publication_day, coalesce(published_at, \\'\\') from items where input_id=?', (a,)).fetchone()) + (a,)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,re,collections; sys.path.insert(0,\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\\\"); import fresh_test as f; p=f.jp; fs=json.loads(f.POOL.read_text()); exposed={(c[\\\"draw\\\"],c[\\\"label\\\"]) for c in json.loads((p.OUT/\\\"cases.json\\\").read_text())}|set(re.findall(r\\\"\"'^### '\"\\\\d+\\\\. (\\\\S+) (Q\\\\d+) \\\",(f.HERE/\\\"census/rejected-answers.md\\\").read_text(),re.M)); ids=json.loads((p.KEYS/\\\"mapping-key-diagnostic.json\\\").read_text()); lib={(d,x[\\\"question_id\\\"]):x for d,l in ids.items() for x in json.loads((p.DIAG/\\\"mapping-out\\\"/(\\\"library-{}.json\\\".format(l))).read_text())}; defn=lambda s: \\\" \\\".join(s.casefold().split()); exqs=collections.defaultdict(list); mapped=collections.defaultdict(set); mm=json.loads((p.DIAG/\\\"mapping-out/mapping.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"mapping\\\"];\nfor x in exposed: exqs[defn(lib[x][\\\"question\\\"])].append(x)\nfor d,m in mm.items():\n for k,vs in m.items():\n  for v in vs:\n   if v[\\\"covers\\\"] is True: mapped[(d,v[\\\"question\\\"])].add(k)\nexm=set.union(set(),*(mapped[x] for x in exposed)); exact=[]; overlap=[]; freshm=collections.Counter(); first=[]\nfor c in fs:\n x=(c[\\\"draw\\\"],c[\\\"label\\\"]); q=lib[x][\\\"question\\\"];\n if defn(q) in exqs: exact.append((x,exqs[defn(q)],q));\n if mapped[x]&exm: overlap.append((x,sorted(mapped[x]&exm),q));\n for m in mapped[x]: freshm[m]+=1\n if not c[\\\"held\\\"]: first.append((x,q))\nprint(\\\"exposed\\\", len(exposed),\\\"locked exact\\\",len(exact),\\\"same matter mapping\\\",len(overlap),\\\"some pooled matter repeated\\\",[(m,n) for m,n in freshm.items() if n>1]); print(\\\"exact\\\",*exact[:8],sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\"); print(\\\"mapped\\\",*overlap[:12],sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\"); print(\\\"moved\\\",first)'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
