{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'F-old-1-Q8|F-old-1-Q25|F-old-3-Q38|F-old-3-Q28' poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/freshpool.json; rg -n 'old-2 Q9|old-1 Q20|old-3 Q37|old-3 Q23' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/rejected-answers.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py | sed -n '376,417p'\"","aggregated_output":"99:  \"case\": \"F-old-1-Q8\",\n312:  \"case\": \"F-old-1-Q25\",\n1158:  \"case\": \"F-old-3-Q28\",\n1222:  \"case\": \"F-old-3-Q38\",\n234:### 24. old-1 Q20 (C175) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n383:### 39. old-2 Q9 (C150) answer-mark=unsupported type=figure\n408:### 42. old-3 Q23 (C143) answer-mark=unsupported type=yes/no\n455:### 47. old-3 Q37 (C174) answer-mark=unsupported type=figure\n   376\t    least 2 of 3 repeats; net target repairs (the arm holds, v7 does not, minus the reverse) at least ceil(5n/13); no control lost; the\n   377\t    arm's refusals, recomputed against the request each answer received on the store as of the stored judgement, not above v7's. An\n   378\t    invalid rung counts as refused and not supported.\"\"\"\n   379\t    key = json.loads(TEST_KEY.read_text())\n   380\t    marks = json.loads((jp.OUT / 'marks-fresh-test.json').read_text())\n   381\t    rows = {c['case']: c for c in json.loads(FRESH.read_text())}\n   382\t    supported = {(m['arm'], m['case'], m['repeat']): (m['marks'] or {}).get('answer') == 'supported' for m in marks.values() if m['kind'] == 'probe'}\n   383\t    invalid = {(c['arm'], c['case'], c['repeat']) for c in key['invalid']}\n   384\t    for item in invalid:\n   385\t        supported[item] = False\n   386\t    arms = (control, arm)\n   387\t    missing = [(a, c, r) for a in arms for c in rows for r in (1, 2, 3) if (a, c, r) not in supported]\n   388\t    if missing:\n   389\t        raise SystemExit(f'{len(missing)} answers not marked, e.g. {missing[:4]}: refused')\n   390\t    refused = Counter()\n   391\t    for a in arms:\n   392\t        for name, case in rows.items():\n   393\t            user = arm_user(stored_request(case['draw'], case['request_sha256'])['messages'][1]['content'], a)\n   394\t            views, _ = jp.store_paths(case['draw'])\n   395\t            for r in (1, 2, 3):\n   396\t                if (a, name, r) in invalid:\n   397\t                    refused[a] += 1\n   398\t                    continue\n   399\t                answer = json.loads((jp.OUT / 'fresh-probe' / a / f'{name}-{r}.json').read_text())['answer']\n   400\t                refused[a] += bool(jp.refusals_before(views, case['view_id'], case['judgement_id'], answer, user))\n   401\t    holds = {a: {c: sum(supported[(a, c, r)] for r in (1, 2, 3)) >= 2 for c in rows} for a in arms}\n   402\t    targets = sorted(c for c in rows if rows[c]['role'] == 'target')\n   403\t    controls = sorted(c for c in rows if rows[c]['role'] == 'control')\n   404\t    repaired = [t for t in targets if holds[arm][t] and not holds[control][t]]\n   405\t    broken = [t for t in targets if holds[control][t] and not holds[arm][t]]\n   406\t    lost = [c for c in controls if holds[control][c] and not holds[arm][c]]\n   407\t    line = math.ceil(5 * len(targets) / 13)\n   408\t    moved = {a: sum(sum(json.loads((jp.OUT / 'fresh-probe' / a / f'{t}-{r}.json').read_text())['answer']['rung'] != rows[t]['rung'] for r in (1, 2, 3)) >= 2\n   409\t                    for t in targets) for a in arms}\n   410\t    report = {'arm': arm, 'targets': len(targets), 'controls': len(controls), 'line': line,\n   411\t              'targets held': {a: sum(holds[a][t] for t in targets) for a in arms}, 'targets moved off the stored rung (2 of 3)': moved,\n   412\t              'controls held': {a: sum(holds[a][c] for c in controls) for a in arms}, 'repaired': repaired, 'broken': broken,\n   413\t              'net': len(repaired) - len(broken), 'controls lost': lost, 'refused': dict(refused),\n   414\t              'plants': {cid: m['marks'] for cid, m in marks.items() if m['kind'] == 'plant'},\n   415\t              'screen passes': len(repaired) - len(broken) >= line and not lost and refused[arm] <= refused[control]}\n   416\t    print(json.dumps(report, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   417\t    (jp.OUT / f'fresh-score-{arm}.json').write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"**Hold the send. The pool contains questions the design already saw, and the scorer can credit an answer production would refuse.**\n\n- **Pool.** I found five exact question repeats and nine cases mapped to previously exposed matters, with some overlap. For example, pooled old-1 Q8 is the same FY2027 Data Center revenue question as exposed old-2 Q9. Exclude exposed matters across draws and count each remaining matter once. The 114/116 unchanged forecasts suit a test of how prior answers carry forward. They limit what the result says about forecasts in general. Paired v7 re-sends help control for selection on rejected answers. [fresh_test.py:83](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py:83) · [freshpool.json:99](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/freshpool.json:99)\n- **Selection.** Both ceilings are reasonable as preset screening ratios on distinct matters. At eight targets, the repair bar rounds to four. The code can proceed below eight or with too few controls. Enforce both prerequisites before sending. [fresh_test.py:240](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py:240)\n- **Wording.** H1 is faithful. It retains the previous forecast and reasons, and changes only their heading. H2’s aim is sourced in PRD 06, although “this evidence” could be read to omit dependencies and themes. Q31’s account explains why it thought it should have stayed after it moved. That single account gives too little reason to send H2. [06-views.md:19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/06-views.md:19) · [Q31 account](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/account/T-new-2-Q31.json:19)\n- **Screen.** Using identical cards preserves blinding. Count every production refusal as unsupported and require the reader controls to pass. Keep forecast moves descriptive. Reasoning can improve within the same range, and v7 can move on a re-send. A whole-window replay before H1 clears the screen would serve no decision. [fresh_test.py:382](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py:382)\n\nDISAGREE: Freeze a genuinely fresh set and fix scoring before sending H1 against v7."}}
